WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.400
With Black Panther, it was different.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:07.190
I felt like I had already won.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:19.230
And so the nomination was like a portal to my really feeling that I was bringing the culture with me.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:29.460
And we were getting a chance to, you know, shout to the world that, you know, this is truth and this is Africa.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.170
This is what my whole career has built up to.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.330
Spike Lee, thank you for my star. I hope this makes you proud.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.880
Marvel may have created the first black superhero,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.400
But through costume design, we turned him into an African King.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:57.960
And so there was a sense already that I was a winner.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:03.720
Just because of the way that the film was embraced when it came out.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.880
But there's something about the fanciful that runs through your work.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.340
That being able to realize it on that scale,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.860
getting to work on those conflict movies,

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.620
The idea of getting some psychological detail in the costume, creating a world must have been,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.700
I think, or at least I wonder if it was especially exciting for you?

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.990
It was especially exciting.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.850
I'm working with some very special directors.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:35.190
When I think about Spike Lee and his understanding of where he wanted us to land.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.620
With Do The Right Thing, he was very conscious.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:44.370
There was purpose in the work and he let us all know that we all had a purpose here.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:48.930
And working with Ryan Coogler is similar in that way.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:56.730
That is so strong and where he's wanting this visual story to land.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.610
Our genius director, Ryan Coogler.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.810
You are a guiding force.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.410
Thank you for your trust in understanding my role in telling the African-American story.

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:22.360
You can't help but be excited and want to join hands and create a purpose for yourself as in your art.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:30.790
So the Okavango Triangle or the the details, the choice of fabrics, the composition,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:39.040
All of that creates the spirit of where we all want people to land when they watch it,

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.670
Where we want the spirit of the film to go.

